      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"In this investigation, the researchers meticulously optimized ionizable lipids within LNP formulations, focusing on pKa modifications to enhance endosomal escape, crucial for cytosolic delivery of mRNA encoding tumor suppressor proteins. The study highlights the significance of alkyl chain lengths in determining the structural stability of LNPs, which directly influences their interaction with the cell membrane, thereby facilitating more efficient intracellular release of therapeutic mRNA. This optimization strategy underscores the potential for targeted cancer therapy through improved delivery mechanisms.\"",
      "source": "target",
